## Statement

Use natural units $c=\hbar=1$ and fix one bundle sector of the adopted massless $\mathcal N=4$ $SU(2)$ Yang–Mills model on the round Euclidean four-sphere $S^4_r$, with $r>0$ a length. The adopted background fixes the action, contour, field content, and total gauge-fixed odd transformation $Q=s+\delta$; on its fields and ghosts the square is $Q^2=\delta_{\rm gauge}(a_0)+\delta_{U(1)}(\omega)$, where the first term is the declared infinitesimal gauge transformation and the second is the selected circle action. This is a physical model assumption, not a deduction that the formal continuum functional integral exists.

For a fixed regulator label $\rho$, assume that a finite-dimensional regulator of this model is supplied by an oriented smooth field-parameter manifold $\mathfrak F_\rho$ of finite dimension $n$, a smooth positive volume form $\mu_\rho$, and integration over the whole cycle $\mathfrak F_\rho$. Let $\mathcal A_\rho=\Omega^\bullet(\mathfrak F_\rho;\mathbb C)$, let $I_\rho(F)=\int_{\mathfrak F_\rho}F_{[n]}$ be the integral of the degree-$n$ part, and let $Q_\rho$ be the induced smooth odd derivation. The regulator must preserve the stated total $Q$ action and its square; no regulator existence or regulator-preservation claim is assumed. Let $J\subseteq\mathbb R$ be a nonempty open interval of dimensionless deformation parameters. Let $S_\rho,O_\rho\in\mathcal A_\rho$ be even, let $V_\rho\in\mathcal A_\rho$ be odd, and define $E_{\rho,t}=e^{-S_\rho-tQ_\rho V_\rho}$. In units with $\hbar=1$, assume the regulated action $S_\rho$ and deformation $tQ_\rho V_\rho$ are dimensionless. Assume $Q_\rho S_\rho=Q_\rho O_\rho=0$ and $(Q_\rho^2V_\rho)E_{\rho,t}=0$ for every $t\in J$. Assume the regulated measure and cycle are Q-invariant on the admissible integrands, in the exact sense that $I_\rho(Q_\rho(O_\rho V_\rho E_{\rho,t}))=0$ for every $t\in J$, with no anomaly or boundary contribution. Write $(O_\rho E_{\rho,t})_{[n]}=f_{\rho,t}\mu_\rho$ and assume $f_{\rho,t}$ is integrable for each $t$, has a measurable parameter derivative almost everywhere, and for every compact $K\subset J$ one $g_K\in L^1(\mathfrak F_\rho,\mu_\rho)$ bounds both $|f_{\rho,t}|$ and $|\partial_t f_{\rho,t}|$ for every $t\in K$ outside one null set. Then

$$Z_\rho(t):=I_\rho(O_\rho E_{\rho,t})$$

is constant on $J$, and for every $t\in J$,

$$Z_\rho'(t)=-I_\rho(O_\rho(Q_\rho V_\rho)E_{\rho,t})=-I_\rho(Q_\rho(O_\rho V_\rho E_{\rho,t}))=0.$$

The conclusion applies only to this fixed finite-dimensional regulator and fixed bundle sector at finite $t$. The adopted S4 postulate does not construct the finite-dimensional data above, and this result supplies no infinite-dimensional continuum identity, $t\to\infty$ localization limit, or regulator-removal theorem.

## Statement references

[[post-qftx-rigid-supersymmetric-background|Adopted S4 model and gauge-fixed Q-square]]

[[def-qftx-supersymmetry-fluctuation-complex|Gauge-fixed fluctuation and regulator data]]

[[thm-finite-dimensional-q-exact-deformation-invariance|Finite-dimensional Q-exact deformation theorem]]

[Pestun, Section 3](https://arxiv.org/pdf/0712.2824)

[Pestun and Zabzine, Section 1](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1608.02953)

[Folland, Theorem 2.27(b)](https://djvu.online/file/NPF4BEtSuqdFA)

[Schwarz and Zaboronsky, Section 3](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9511112)

[Peelaers, Sections 1.1–1.2](https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/3026/attachments/2163/2457/Peelaers-LectureNotes.pdf)

## Facts & Assumptions

**Given:** The adopted S4 model and its total gauge-fixed Q transformation, together with one fixed finite-dimensional regulator whose field algebra, integral, Q-closure, Q-squared condition, vanishing Q-boundary integral, and compact-parameter majorants satisfy the Statement.

[A1] [[post-qftx-rigid-supersymmetric-background]]: the adopted model is the source-qualified Euclidean massless $\mathcal N=4$ $SU(2)$ theory on round $S^4_r$; its total gauge-fixed transformation is $Q=s+\delta$ and its square on fields and ghosts is $\delta_{\rm gauge}(a_0)+\delta_{U(1)}(\omega)$. The source's functional measure and S4 noncommutative regulator extension remain formal assumptions.

[F1] [[def-qftx-susy-background-data]]: the supplied rigid background records the spin/R/gauge bundles, off-shell transformation, contour, gauge-fixing and ghost data, and regulator or measure inputs; it does not construct a continuum measure.

[F2] [[def-qftx-supersymmetry-fluctuation-complex]]: a finite-dimensional regulator is extra data consisting of a finite-dimensional oriented field manifold, volume form, cycle, graded differential-form algebra, top-degree integral, and an induced odd derivation with its exact square.

[A2] The regulator is fixed in one bundle sector and obeys every integrability, Q-closure, Q-squared, Q-invariance, anomaly, boundary, and majorant condition stated above. This is a conditional finite-model hypothesis, not a claim that the source's formal S4 regulator has been constructed in this form.

[F3] [[thm-finite-dimensional-q-exact-deformation-invariance]]: for finite-dimensional differential-form integration data with $QS=QO=0$, $(Q^2V)e^{-S-tQV}=0$, zero Q-boundary integral, and a compact-parameter integrable majorant for the integrand and derivative, $I(Oe^{-S-tQV})$ is constant at finite parameter values and has derivative $-I(O(QV)e^{-S-tQV})=-I(Q(OVe^{-S-tQV}))=0$.

## Proof

1.1 By [A1], the physical input fixes the S4 background and the total gauge-fixed Q-square but does not assert nilpotency. The background definition [F1] says a formal measure is not a constructed measure. Under [A2], $Q_\rho$ is the regulator-preserving realization of that transformation, and the required Q-squared condition is imposed on $V_\rho E_{\rho,t}$. [given, A1, A2, F1]

1.2 By [F2], the regulator's field manifold, graded algebra, top-degree integral, and odd derivation have exactly the finite-dimensional form required by [F3]. The remaining hypotheses of [F3] are precisely $Q_\rho S_\rho=Q_\rho O_\rho=0$, $(Q_\rho^2V_\rho)E_{\rho,t}=0$, the zero-boundary Q-invariance identity, and the stated compact-parameter integrable majorant. [given, F2, F3]

2.1 Apply [F3] to these data. It gives $Z_\rho'(t)=-I_\rho(O_\rho(Q_\rho V_\rho)E_{\rho,t})=-I_\rho(Q_\rho(O_\rho V_\rho E_{\rho,t}))=0$ for every $t\in J$, and states that $Z_\rho$ is constant on $J$. This is a conditional deduction for the fixed finite regulator and sector only. [F3, step 1.2] ∎
