        "statement": "Let $M=T^2$ be a closed flat Euclidean two-torus. Fix two nondynamical $U(1)$ background connections $A_1,A_2$, each a globally defined real 1-form on the trivial bundle, and allow only gauge transformations $A_i\\mapsto A_i+d\\lambda_i$ with smooth single-valued periodic real functions $\\lambda_i$. Use natural units $c=\\hbar=1$, so $[A_i]=$ mass and the functional below is dimensionless. In a declared counterterm scheme, take the allowed local background counterterm\n\n$$\nC_k[A_1,A_2]=\\frac{ik}{2\\pi}\\int_{T^2} A_1\\wedge A_2,\n$$\n\nwhere $k\\in\\mathbb R$ is a fixed dimensionless coefficient. Suppose an exact background-coupled RG comparison has $W_{\\mathrm{UV}}[A_1,A_2]=W_{\\mathrm{IR}}[A_1,A_2]+C_k[A_1,A_2]$ on this background domain. Then the two local anomaly representatives differ by\n\n$$\n\\delta C_k=\\frac{ik}{2\\pi}\\int_{T^2}\\bigl(-\\lambda_1 F_2+\\lambda_2 F_1\\bigr),\\qquad F_i=dA_i,\n$$\n\nand therefore define the same local anomaly class modulo the declared counterterms.",
